      "id": 1,
      "options": {
        "content": "**Source:** `mm/observability/subscribers.py` + in-process `/metrics` (`mm/observability/registry.py`).\n\n**If charts are empty:**\n1. **Scrape:** Prometheus targets `host.docker.internal:8000` (see `docker/prometheus.yml`). The **runtime must run on the host** with `metrics_enabled` / port **8000** (or set `MM_METRICS_PORT` and change Prometheus). In Prometheus UI → **Status → Targets**, `market_maker` should be **UP**.\n2. **Histogram rows** stay empty until you have **execution sync** traffic (`mm_order_sync_latency_ms_*`, `mm_frame_to_exec_*` buckets need observations).\n3. **Logs (Loki):** Relative `log_path` is resolved to the **repo** `logs/` directory so Alloy’s `./logs` mount sees lines. Restart runtime after upgrading.\n\n**Rates:** `rate(...[$__rate_interval])` — legacy and joint strategy frames, controller decisions, sync rounds, venue place/cancel accept counts.\n\n**Latencies (histograms):** `mm_frame_to_exec_sync_latency_ms` = wall ms from frame `created_at_ms` to `ExecutionSyncRequested`; `mm_market_window_end_to_exec_sync_latency_ms` = sync timestamp − local `t_end_ms`; `mm_order_sync_latency_ms` = completed order-manager sync latency; legacy paths fall back to sync request → next `execution:state` snapshot.\n\n**Joint frame gauges:** `mm_joint_strategy_frames_total`, `mm_latency_skew_ms`, `mm_frame_*_ready`, `mm_frame_ledger_fresh`.\n\n**Gauges (last scrape):** `mm_order_sync_create_count` / `mm_order_sync_cancel_count` (per sync batch), controller latency gauge, live orders.",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
      "title": "Notes",
      "transparent": true,
      "type": "text"
    },
